{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546022-how-would-we-adapt-silent-hill-to-curseborne","id":1546022,"title":"How would we adapt Silent Hill to Curseborne?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-17T04:45:29-08:00","id":1546022,"title":"How would we adapt Silent Hill to Curseborne?","content":"Basically, the premise.<br /> <br /> If we were doing Silent Hill as a setting in Curseborne then how would all of the various supernatural critters and characters be adapted.<br /> <br /> What is the place?<br /> <br /> I think it'd be fun to speculate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T06:51:21-08:00","id":1546027,"title":"","content":"<br /> On the one hand I do like to advocate for using the right game for the right purpose, but the question here isn't &quot;what game is the best choice for doing a Silent Hill adaptation&quot;, it's &quot;what's the best way to run Silent Hill in Curseborne&quot;, being asked on the Curseborne forums, so it's okay for the choice of game system to be baked in.<br /> <br /> Like if the question was &quot;how would you run <i>Vampire Diaries</i> in Curseborne&quot; I wouldn't reply by saying &quot;don't, just run Monsterhearts&quot; and if the question was &quot;how do you run an all-Hungry game&quot; I wouldn't reply &quot;don't, just run Requiem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I will say that you raise a perfectly reasonable point about the fact that Silent Hill assumes mortal protagonists with limited knowledge of the supernatural but this ties into the wider issue that, frankly, a <i>lot</i> of Curseborne's implied (or indeed outright stated) inspirations actually assume mortal protagonists with relatively limited experience of supernatural phenomena.<br /> <br /> In fact in some ways this makes &quot;how do you do <i>Silent Hill</i> in Curseborne&quot; a really interesting question because Silent Hill clearly *is* an inspiration for the game but, as you say, Silent Hill doesn't assume a supernatural protagonist.<br /> <br /> And thinking about it, the answer to the Silent Hill question highlights a lot of what's different about the game because I think the answer to the question &quot;how do you adapt Silent Hill to Curseborne&quot; is &quot;remember that in this game, the protagonist is <i>Mary</i> Sunderland&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 11-18-2024, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T08:25:05-08:00","id":1546031,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can adapt Silent Hill as presented in its games, to Curseborne. <br /> <br /> Silent Hill is a supernatural realm that takes on aspects of the troubled pysches of those who come into it. Very few of the Silent Hill protagonists have been psychologically healthy individuals in the wrong place at the wrong time. <br /> <br /> So having werewolves, demons, vampires and ghosts show up takes a lot of the horror out of the setting in terms of facing your own personal demons. <br /> <br /> The monsters in Silent Hill tend to be weak as well since normal people are the ones that deal with them. <br /> <br /> Now all that being said, you could have Curseborne interact with Silent Hill from an outsiders perspective. <br /> <br /> It's obviously a liminality of some kind. Curseborne investigating the town while mortals are trapped in it, and figuring out the &quot;creatures&quot; in it are being generated from the subconscious trauma of those mortals is a plot that could be done. <br /> <br /> Then there is the history of the town itself and all the cult stuff it's founders got up to. <br /> <br /> But the Accursed themselves wouldn't make good candidates for being victims of Silent Hill. Particularly in comparison to the monsters of COD and WOD. <br /> <br /> I think this has to do with the lack of a morality mechanic in Curseborne. In Cod every splat has a morality they have to watch, to make sure they don't lose control. A heavy part of those games is your morality and not becoming a complete monster. <br /> <br /> Curseborne doesn't have that built in, so playing on the subconscious morality of the Curseborne is less helpful because a Gaki doesn't have to worry about losing their morality from eating Souls. <br /> <br /> Which means Silent Hill effectively becomes a dungeon or problem to solve for The Curseborne rather than an issue to face. <br /> <br /> Personally I think Silent Hill is a poor adaptation for The Accursed because of all this. <br /> <br /> However, I think Resident Evil and it's lore and monsters *WOULD* fit perfectly into Curseborne by contrast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T09:11:52-08:00","id":1546033,"title":"","content":"I don't think the lack of a morality meter is an issue here. Humans in the Curseborne setting don't have an Integrity stat either, I don't think that can be taken to imply that everybody in the setting is an amoral sociopath who never regrets anything.<br /> <br /> It's true that default Curseborne characters seem *likely* to be a lot less tortured than default characters in CofD (although often that element of the *of Darkness games was a bit nominal) in that you're potentially going to be playing somebody who just straight eats souls and doesn't feel bad about it, but that's going to vary a fair bit from table to table and it seems like at least half the time the expected position of PCs is &quot;the shit my family does is messed up&quot; not &quot;the shit my family does is completely normal and cool.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T10:36:11-08:00","id":1546035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>We don't </b>- we take <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> corebook and use <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">CoD </a><a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/FanBooks/Silent_Hill.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Silent Hill</i> fan book</b></a> - and play with mortal characters, like <b>Silent Hill</b> franchise was envisioned to be played. \ud83d\ude09 ( <b>Curseborne </b>do not have any mortal investigators rules. And I suspect it will not get /if any / before <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543052-curseborne-supplement-idea-%E2%80%93-mortal-hunters\">Hunters equivalent supplement for <b>CB</b> gameline</a>. )<br /> <br /> I know <b>CTPhillips</b> you are now in a nerd phase on <b>CB </b>- but you should adopt game franchineses to game that are closet to original source material. And <b>Silent Hill</b> games are direct corrolation to <b>CoD Mortal</b> games, simple as that. ( And I mean <b>Mortals</b> -<b><i>not </i>Hunters</b> - various protagonists of <b>Silent Hill</b> games are<i> 'ordinary people, confronted with supernatural for a first time'</i> - that is definition of playing strictly Mortals game. Only in on <b>SH</b> game you played soldier- and he still was not proper Hunter in my book. )<br /> <br /> I myself run 2 <b>Silent Hill</b> one-shots on this fun supplement and <b>nWoD/CoD</b> 1E corebook, years ago. \ud83d\ude0e</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, I don't think that remotely works.<br /> <br /> Curseborne is the best for being PHYSICALLY able to run Silent Hill. As in describing phenomenon about Shattered Spaces, Liminarities, and so on.<br /> <br /> The issue about mortal protagonists is being set aside in my mind for this.<br /> <br /> Because I totally believe you can torture monsters psychologically too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T11:53:31-08:00","id":1546039,"title":"","content":"If I had to discuss the issue, I'd actually think Silent Hill makes the perfect sort of place to CREATE Curseborne as opposed to run Curseborne through it. Harry Mason, Cheryl, James, and others being creates who emerge from the hellish psychological adventure scarred but changed. Basically, you could easily run a Silent Hill Shattered Space as a way to make the monsters the PCs have to be afterward.<br /> <br /> An origin story so to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-17-2024, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T15:13:06-08:00","id":1546052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1546022-how-would-we-adapt-silent-hill-to-curseborne?p=1546039#post1546039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to discuss the issue, I'd actually think Silent Hill makes the perfect sort of place to CREATE Curseborne as opposed to run Curseborne through it. Harry Mason, Cheryl, James, and others being creates who emerge from the hellish psychological adventure scarred but changed. Basically, you could easily run a Silent Hill Shattered Space as a way to make the monsters the PCs have to be afterward.<br /> <br /> An origin story so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this and your previous post highlight the problem.<br /> <br /> I think you can make a pretty reasonable case that Curseborne is the White Wolf / Onyx Path setting which is best set up for Silent Hill, the town, being a town that exists. As you say, Liminalities and Shattered spaces seem 100% set up for doing Silent Hill shit it's like their whole deal. The expanded cosmologies of CofD and WoD can produce similar effects but it feels like Silent Hill is a direct influence on the whole concept of Liminalities (or maybe that Silent Hill and Curseborne both have similar influences).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, Curseborne, not having any rules for mortal protagonists, is a terrible fit for running a scenario that feels like Silent Hill <i>the game</i>. Yes, you can psychologically torment monster PCs but I think that's forcing a bit of a square peg into a round hole. Like if you're already a vampire having a creepy house slowly drop hints that it knows you might have done some bad things loses a lot of its bite. Either you're already tormented by the guilt of your existence because that's the kind of vampire you are, or else you're more of the eatin' hearts and takin' names kind of vampire in which case attempting to make you engage with psychological horror will just be annoying out of character.<br /> <br /> This is why I think the way to engage with that kind of source material is to come at it from the PoV of the town, the cult and the monsters. Like there are PC splats that exactly specialise in setting up Silent Hill style scenarios (or at least Silent Hill 2 style scenarios).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-17T17:15:06-08:00","id":1546056,"title":"","content":"Agreed, Silent Hill could absolutely exist in Curseborne but trying to exactly recreate a Silent Hill story would be hard. You could run an Accursed through a Silent Hill story, since they're not immune to Shattered Spaces or anything, but the impression I get is that most Accursed beyond the greenest ones have an idea of what's up with Shattered Spaces and would go &quot;oh, I'm in a Shattered Space, I need to do xyz to beat it.&quot; Similar to how monster hunters go &quot;oh, I'm in a slasher movie/Zombie flick/Ghost story; I need to do xyz to survive and win.&quot; You could tweak it, stronger monsters, or give it a twist like it's some kind of psychological trial thing that an Archon set up, to introduce something that the Accursed would find scary, or something like the opposite of a loophole, a place that supercharges Curses, Damnations, Torments etc.<br /> You could also present a Silent Hill-type place as someplace that your Accursed could move into or use as a safe harbor. It sucks, but being cursed sucks in general and this place has rules you can work around and use to your advantage if you figure it out.<br /> <br /> You could also, now that I think about it, have someone that the Accursed care about get stuck in Silent Hill, and they'd be trying to get them out or at least help somehow, hopefully while preventing the victim from coming out Accursed themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}